# Terraform Provider Docker Compose

[![Release](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/rsbh/terraform-provider-docker-compose)](https://github.com/rsbh/terraform-provider-docker-compose/releases)
[![Go Report Card](https://goreportcard.com/badge/github.com/rsbh/terraform-provider-docker-compose)](https://goreportcard.com/report/github.com/rsbh/terraform-provider-docker-compose)
[![License: MPL 2.0](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MPL%202.0-brightgreen.svg)](LICENSE)

A Terraform provider that manages Docker Compose stacks on remote hosts via SSH.

## Features

- Deploy Docker Compose stacks to remote hosts
- Manage compose files remotely via SSH
- Track and update running containers
- Clean up resources on destroy

## Requirements

- Terraform >= 1.0
- Go >= 1.21 (for building)
- Docker and Docker Compose on the remote host

## Installation

```hcl
terraform {
  required_providers {
    docker-compose = {
      source = "rsbh/docker-compose"
    }
  }
}
```

## Usage

```hcl
provider "docker-compose" {
  host             = "your-server.com"
  user             = "ubuntu"
  private_key_path = "~/.ssh/id_rsa"
}

resource "docker-compose_stack" "app" {
  name     = "myapp"
  work_dir = "/opt/myapp"

  compose_file = <<-EOT
    version: '3.8'
    services:
      web:
        image: nginx:latest
        ports:
          - "80:80"
  EOT
}
```

## Provider Configuration

| Attribute | Description | Required |
|-----------|-------------|----------|
| `host` | SSH host address | Yes |
| `user` | SSH username | Yes |
| `port` | SSH port (default: 22) | No |
